{title: Bow My Knees Before The Father}
{subtitle: Ephesians 3:14–15}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 76}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb/D] | [Eb] | [Gm7] [Bb/F] |
| [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I stand in the light [Eb]of your grace
[Gm7]With boldness I find [Eb]in your face
[Bb]No fear in my [Eb]heart any more
[Cm7]I come to you [F7sus4]with quiet prayer
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]I bow [Bbmaj7/D]my knees before the [Eb]Father
[Gm]From whom every [Bbmaj7/D]family is [Eb]named
In [Gm7]heaven above and on [F]earth [Gm7]below
Your [Eb]name is the [F]one that re[Bb]mains [Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Not faint from the weight [Eb]of the cost
[Gm7]For this is the [Eb]glory I lost
[Bb]And found in the [Eb]strength of your hand
[Cm7]Where you love [F]and where you stand
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]I bow [Bb/D]my knees before the [Eb]Father
[Gm]From whom every [Bbmaj7/D]family is [Eb]named
In [Gm]heaven above and on [F]earth [Gm7]below
Your [Eb]name is the [F]one that re[Bb]mains
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Gm7]Riches of [F/A]glory pour [Eb]out
[Gm7]Strength in the [F/A]spirit and [Eb]doubt
[Gm7]You grant me [F/A]the power to [Eb]be
[Cm7]Rooted and grounded in [Fsus4][F]thee
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]I bow [Bb/D]my knees before the [Eb]Father
[Gm7]From whom every [Bb/D]family is [Eb]named
In [Gm7]heaven above and on [F]earth [Gm7]below
Your [Eb]name is the [Fsus4]one that re[Bb]mains
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Gm7]Bow my [Bbmaj7/D]knees before the Fa[Eb]ther
Your [Cm7]name is the [Fsus4]one that re[Bb][Bb/D]mains
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
